name o3-10-october-six-1
timeout 700
time 1973-10-06T12:30:00Z

# CAMPAIGN O3, SORTIE 10 OF 10 - YOM KIPPUR 1973: GROUND ATTACK IN CONTESTED AIRSPACE.
# THE OPENING STRIKE. THIS FILE IS THE CHAIN TERMINUS: it inherits o3-09-two-fronts.fbm's strike force
# (yxa..yxh) and its umbrella (yxnod / yxsa3 / yxsa6), so whoever the first wave lost is not here and
# whatever it expended is not aboard. It has no controlled sibling - a chain step never does (O1's rule).
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/o3-yom-kippur-1973.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
#
# THE ANCHOR, and it is this campaign's whole reason for existing: at ~14:00 on 6 October 1973 about 220
# Egyptian aircraft - MiG-21, Su-7, MiG-17, Hawker Hunter - struck command posts, observation points,
# artillery positions, armour and fortifications east of the canal, with NO OPPOSITION FROM THE ISRAELI
# AIR FORCE and LIGHT LOSSES [T4/T1]. This file is that shape at 1/18 scale: twelve Red aircraft in two
# layers, eight aim points, the crossing's own missile umbrella overhead, and four Israeli fighters that
# are simply TOO FAR AWAY at t = 0.
#
# THE SPEC'S OWN QUESTION, verbatim: "Can FlightBox reproduce a strike that succeeds because the defender
# was late - which is a statement about spawn timing, not about flying?" That framing is exactly right
# and it is why the CAP here is not weaker, not blinder and not worse-armed than in sortie 09. It is 85
# km away instead of 45. There is no schedule in this format (`C2`: the clock is a stamp, not a trigger;
# `C15`: no time-on-target), so LATENESS IS A DISTANCE and this file makes it one, out loud.
#
# THE SUBSTITUTION AND ITS DIRECTION (stated in every O3 file), and the capstone is where it costs most.
# The MiG-29 stands in for the MiG-17 / Su-7 / Su-20 / MiG-21, whose own catalogue rows are ALPHA and may
# not answer a campaign question - here it plays BOTH the fighter-bomber (low, silent, FAB-500) and the
# top cover (high, radiating, R-27R/R-73), so the anchor's own layer DIFFERENCE is erased.
#   DIRECTION: the ATTACKER is materially STRONGER than history in both layers. This is a strike by
#   twelve fourth-generation fighters, and the anchor's was not. SO IF THIS FILE REPRODUCES "the strike
#   succeeded and losses were light", THAT IS NOT A VALIDATION OF 1973 - it is the weaker statement that
#   a much better force also gets through. A BAD result here would have been the interesting one.
# The Israeli CAP is `f16` (the real defenders flew F-4, Mirage and A-4): Blue is stronger too.
# The umbrella is not substituted; three positions stand for >200, and no `sa2` is present because
# o3-04 MEASURED that an S-75's 450 m floor cannot engage anything at O3's forced 300 m.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE STAGES AND WHAT IT DOES NOT, before any number below. The anchor has FIVE antagonists
# for this strike and this file stages TWO:
#   staged:      the Israeli fighter layer (as F-16s, arriving late) and the crossing's own SAM umbrella
#                (as three netted positions with no IFF)
#   NOT staged:  the Hawk batteries and the scattered AAA that actually produced the anchor's "light
#                losses" - there is no Hawk row in doc/modules/ground/catalogue.md and o3-08 measured
#                that the one gun row that exists lands zero hits on a 231 m/s crosser
#   NOT staged:  the ~100 Mi-8 assault helicopters (`C7`) and the 208 other aircraft (scale)
#   NOT staged:  terrain (`C4`, `--elev const`) - the Sinai here is a 0 m plane
#
# THE ARENA (all coordinates [SET]). Suez sector, `--elev const`, 0 m datum, no terrain masking (C4).
#   the strike    yxa..yxh, 300 m, 450 kt, on a 20.0 km front from 30.70 to 30.88 N, each 6.02 km due
#                 west of ITS OWN aim point at 32.62000 E, straight finals only (o3-03 and attribution
#                 A2 measured what a dog-leg costs, and o3-03 what a long leg costs)
#   the aim points six `target_soft` (artillery and observation positions) plus TWO `target_hard`
#                 (a command post and a fortification) - the anchor's own five-item target list, mapped
#                 onto the two fragility classes this tree has
#   the top cover yxk1..yxk4, 5 000 m, radiating, 14.1 km behind the strikers [DERIVED]
#   the umbrella  yxnod / yxsa3 / yxsa6, `emcon free`, node `wcs free` - o3-04's policy, so the
#                 fratricide channel is OPEN at twelve friendly aircraft
#   the CAP       yx0b1..yx0b4 at 5 000 m on the 33.45000 E line: 79.3 km east of the aim points and
#                 85.3 km from the strikers at t = 0. Head-on closure to the cover is 463 m/s, so the
#                 earliest possible merge is t = 158 s [DERIVED] against a release at t ~ 26 s
# Scale: 1 deg lat = 111 132 m, 1 deg lon at 30.80 N = 95 619 m [DERIVED].
#
# WHY NOTHING DECLARES `survive`, `protect` OR `avoid zone` HERE. All three are DEFERRED objectives whose
# violation is a DECIDING FAILURE, and `missions/FBMissionRunner` ends the whole run at the first one -
# in a 25-unit file that would delete twenty-four units' story at the first casualty. The two zones are
# declared anyway, because a `zone` with no objective still writes `zone_<name>_in`/`zone_<name>_s` per
# judged unit and `zone ENTER`/`EXIT` events, so the exposure is MEASURED without being judged.
# Attrition is therefore read off `UNIT_RESULT` and `campaign ATTRITION`, and the strike is read off
# W3's metric - STRIKERS THAT REACHED RELEASE.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: CAN A STRIKE SUCCEED IN THIS TREE BECAUSE THE DEFENDER WAS LATE, AND WHAT IS
# THE CARRIED FIRST WAVE WORTH?
#
# MEASURED (2026-07-30, --elev const, campaign step 10, fingerprint d73b57fd0e8ddbe0, exit 1):
#   25 units and 48 actors, 160.7 s of sim in 4.1 s of wall clock.
#   THE CARRY: 8 x `campaign CARRY unit=yx? action=stores store=fab500 station=6` - every one of
#     o3-09's strikers comes back with ONE FAB-500 instead of two, because it dropped the other one
#     three hours earlier. NO unit was dropped: sortie 09 lost nobody, which is itself one of this
#     campaign's findings (four AIM-120 arrived inside their own 10 m fuze there and killed nothing).
#   8 OF 8 STRIKERS REACHED RELEASE at t = 26.2, `aimErrM` 46.37-59.59 m.
#   6 OF 8 AIM POINTS DESTROYED - all six `target_soft`, neither `target_hard`. THE SPEC'S BAR (>= 6 of 8)
#     IS MET EXACTLY, AND IT IS MET AT THE CEILING: the two that live are the two the store provably
#     cannot kill (o3-02: 12.1 m needed, 66 m delivered), so 6 of 8 is not a good score, it is the ONLY
#     score this loadout can produce.
#   10 OF 12 RED AIRCRAFT RECOVERED (the spec's bar was >= 9 of 12); zero Blue losses. `yxd` at t = 127.8
#     and `yxk3` at t = 160.6.
#   THE CAP SAW AT ONCE AND COULD NOT REACH: first Blue `radar RADAR_CONTACT` at t = 3.9 s at 45.16 nm
#     (83.6 km) with elDeg -4.x - it had the low strikers from the first sweep - and first `sms RELEASE`
#     at t = 148.4 s, 122.2 s AFTER THE LAST BOMB WAS ALREADY ON THE GROUND. SO "LATE" IN THIS TREE IS
#     NOT A DETECTION FACT, IT IS A CLOSURE FACT: 85 km of separation buys the whole strike, and it buys
#     it against a defender who was watching the entire time.
#   AND THE ONE THING THE FRIENDLY UMBRELLA FINALLY DID: `stores DETONATION unit=yxsa6_3m9_13
#     target=yxd missM=4.73732 fuzeM=8` at t = 127.8, fluxJm2 191 540, `damage KILL unit=yxd reason=
#     "combat ineffective"`. THE CROSSING'S OWN 2K12 SHOT DOWN ONE OF ITS OWN STRIKERS. Seven launches,
#     all seven at its own aircraft, and the second 3M9 arrived. That is the fratricide channel of
#     o3-04 / o3-05 / o3-06 / o3-09 finally closing, at the fifth attempt and on the biggest file.
#   -> YES: A STRIKE SUCCEEDS BECAUSE THE DEFENDER WAS LATE, and in this tree "late" is purely a
#      distance. And the honest half of that sentence is that ALMOST nothing else in this file could have
#      stopped it either - the store decided the target list before anybody flew, the gun layer is
#      absent, and the only Red aircraft that fell to a surface-to-air round fell to its OWN.
#
# AND THE CARRY IS THE MOST DECISIVE ONE IN THE EIGHT BUILT CAMPAIGNS, which is not what was expected of
# it. Run STANDALONE (attribution A4, fingerprint 0e7a46e6a4277174, exit 2) the same file has 16 FAB-500
# instead of 8, and:
#   telemetry            0 OF 48 FILES BYTE-IDENTICAL. W3's carried node left 30 of 58 identical and
#                        moved no trajectory column; this carry changes the MASS AND THE LATERAL BALANCE
#                        of eight aircraft, so the physics diverge at the first substep.
#   `aimAcrossM`         +48.31...+48.37 m with two stores  ->  -39.11...-39.22 m with one.
#                        AN 87.5 M SWING, AND THE SIGN FLIPS. A single store on the left inboard pylon
#                        with its mirror station empty is a lateral asymmetry, and the standing
#                        cross-track offset this airframe already has (yaw channel measured OFF,
#                        doc/modules/mig29/module.md gap 4i) reverses under it. The swing is LARGER than
#                        the FAB-500's own 68.4 m kill radius.
#   `aimErrM`            54.01-66.39 m -> 46.37-59.59 m; mean 60.0 -> 55.4 m, and NOT uniformly: three
#                        aircraft got worse by 3.7-4.4 m and five better by 9.6-10.1 m. The campaign
#                        does not claim a uniform improvement.
#   aim points killed    6 of 8 in BOTH runs. The swing is big enough to move the miss to the other side
#                        of the target and still not big enough to change a verdict.
#   Red losses           2 (yxd to its OWN 2K12, yxk3 to an AIM-120) -> 2 (yxf, yxh, both to AIM-120 at
#                        0.19 and 0.84 m, at t = 385.8 and 382.2). SAME COUNT, DIFFERENT AIRCRAFT, AND A
#                        DIFFERENT CAUSE: standalone, the 2K12's three 3M9 all MISS.
#   run length           160.7 s -> 398.8 s; exit 1 -> exit 2
#   -> SO ONE UNEXPENDED BOMB IS WORTH ONE AIRCRAFT AND 238 SECONDS OF RUN, and the aircraft it is worth
#      was killed by its own side's missile. That is `carry stores` doing something no other campaign in
#      the set has measured it doing.
#
# READING RULE: exit 1 = FAIL is the EXPECTED shape AS A CAMPAIGN STEP and it is not a defect: the run
# ends when a Red aircraft with no objectives of its own becomes combat-ineffective (`yxk3` at t = 160.7),
# which is a deciding failure. STANDALONE the same file gives exit 2 = CRASH, because the aircraft that
# falls there reaches the ground first. NEITHER CODE IS THE VERDICT. THE MEASUREMENT
# is, in this order: (1) every `campaign CARRY` line (this file's only source of inherited state);
# (2) strikers that reached release with their `aimErrM`; (3) which of the eight aim points died, BY
# CLASS; (4) the first Blue `radar RADAR_CONTACT` and the first Blue `sms RELEASE`, against the release
# tick; (5) every `site LAUNCH` attributed to a callsign; (6) `UNIT_RESULT` for all twelve Red aircraft.
# Read standalone, this file has 16 stores instead of 8 and that difference is the campaign - and it is
# worth an aircraft, measured above and in doc/campaigns/o3-yom-kippur-1973.md §State (attribution run
# A4). exit 0 is impossible: the two hardened aim points can never be killed.

zone umbrella 30.84000 32.31000 35000 100 18000
zone ceiling  30.80000 32.45000 90000 2200 20000

net crossing
  control yxnod
  link wire
  period 4.0
  hold 3
  wcs free
  member yxnod
  member yxsa3
  member yxsa6

# ---- THE STRIKE: eight aircraft, eight aim points, one 20.0 km front ----
unit yxa
  module mig29
  team hostile
  flight wave 1
  spawn 30.74000 32.55700 300 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_emission off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 fab500
  set store 6 fab500
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode opt
  wp 30.74000 32.62000 300 450
  wp 30.68000 32.30000 300 450
  objective kill unit yx0t1

